# Better GHub - Project Rules

## Project Overview

This is a **Chrome Extension (Manifest V3)** that enhances GitHub Pull Request workflow. It uses **TypeScript** with **esbuild** for bundling and **ES modules** for imports.

## Code Style

### TypeScript Standards

- Use strict TypeScript (tsconfig strict mode enabled)
- Target ES2021
- Use `import/export` syntax (ES modules)
- Use single quotes for strings
- Always end statements with semicolons

### Module Exports

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - named exports
export class CacheManager { }
export const Octicons = { };

// ✅ GOOD - functional API
export async function getCurrentUser() { }
```

## File Structure

```
src/
  api/              - GitHub API (folder with index.ts)
    index.ts        - re-exports all API functions
    client.ts       - base HTTP client
    metrics.ts      - API call tracking
    get-*.ts        - individual request files
  
  constants.ts      - app constants (VERSION, etc.)
  content.ts        - content script for PR pages
  dashboard.ts      - dashboard script for GitHub home
  background.ts     - service worker
  i18n.ts           - internationalization
  oauth.ts          - GitHub OAuth flow
  pr-service.ts     - PR analysis and processing
  types.ts          - all TypeScript interfaces
  ui.ts             - UI components (loader, tooltip, etc.)
  utils.ts          - utilities (cache, token, DOM helpers)

popup/              - Extension popup UI
options/            - Extension options page
dist/               - Built output (gitignored)
```

## File Size Rules

### When to Split Files

- **Split a file** if it exceeds ~300 lines or has multiple unrelated responsibilities
- **Create a folder** with the same name as the file
- **Add index.ts** that re-exports all parts
- **One responsibility per file** - e.g., one API request per file

### Example: Splitting a Large File

If `api.ts` becomes too large:

```
src/api.ts (300+ lines)  →  src/api/
                              index.ts          # exports all
                              client.ts         # base client
                              get-user.ts       # GET /user
                              get-pr-data.ts    # GET /repos/.../pulls
                              search-issues.ts  # GET /search/issues
```

### File Size Guidelines

| File Type | Max Lines | Action if exceeded |
|-----------|-----------|-------------------|
| Utility files | ~200 | Split by category |
| Components | ~150 | Extract sub-components |
| API files | ~100 | One request per file |
| Type files | ~200 | Split by domain |

## Build System

- **Bundler**: esbuild
- **Build command**: `npm run build`
- **Watch mode**: `npm run build:watch`
- **Type check**: `npm run typecheck`
- Output goes to `dist/` directory

## Chrome Extension Specifics

- Load extension from `dist/` folder after building
- Content scripts are bundled into single files
- Use `chrome.storage` for persistent data
- Use `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` for background communication

## i18n

- All user-facing strings must use i18n system
- Locales: `_locales/en/` (primary), `_locales/pl/`
- Use `__MSG_keyName__` in manifest.json
- Use `i18n.getMessage('keyName')` or `msg('keyName')` in TypeScript
- HTML files use `__MSG_keyName__` translated at runtime by `translatePage()`

## Testing

- Tests go in `tests/` directory with `.test.ts` suffix
- Use Jest with ts-jest preset
- Run tests with `npm test`

## Git Rules

- **NEVER push changes to the repository** - only commit locally, user will push manually
- **NEVER run `git push`** under any circumstances
- Only create commits when explicitly asked by the user

## Before Committing

1. Run `npm run build` - ensure build succeeds
2. Run `npm run typecheck` - fix TypeScript errors
3. Run `npm run lint` - fix any lint errors
4. Run `npm test` - ensure tests pass
